

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 6, TURN 2

                                  FOR

                                 LUCKY

  You missed the turn deadline. The computer ordered Defend actions for your
generals. If we receive a late move, we will process it and send you the turn
results. If you miss 2 turns, the computer will drop you from the game.





  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  Winter melted into spring, and Lucky made ready to carry out his urgent 
orders.  He prepared his armies to defend Mato Grosso and the surrounding 
provinces.

    After a hard year of campaigning, you throw a party for your generals.   
As  you step out the back of your royal tent for some air, you hear a 
rustling  in the nearby bushes.    You whip out your sword and cock your arm 
for a  swing, just as a bewildered swears a helm much too big for his head, 
carries a long flimsy willow branch,  and the Sword Excalibur hangs 
precariously from his worn-out hemp belt."     Ho!    Hey!    Hi!    Tis I, 
Bushrager Quintilian, Shrublord of the first Super  World,", he chatters as 
he I see much potential in you, so I come in hopes of helping you bring 
honor  and prosperity back to the Bush Folk of this land!    You must expand 
like the  branches of the Dogwood, hold your land like the roots of an Alder 
in the  bog, and become strong likone-- Lead yur troops to the call: 'Give m 
Rhododendrons or give me Death!     '"
  If Quintilian searches a feature, any monetary treasure Quintilian 
captures will be given to you.  If Quintilian captures a magic treasure, 
Quintilian will give it to your King when he departs for Valhalla, or you 
can order Quintilian to Give it to one of your characters.  You can do 
anything you want with the magic item Quintilian came with, but the item 
will leave at the end of his stay with you.  Except for the rules given in 
this paragraph, Quintilian can generally be treated just like your other 
Heroes, and can be affected by any spell except Resurrection.  The main 
limitation in using Quintilian is that Quintilian has only enough patience 
to practice with you for one of the phase(s) Quintilian is with you.  
Quintilian will leave at the end of the last phase Quintilian is scheduled 
to serve you, after all battles have been fought.  Quintilian can lead 
armies, but when Quintilian returns to Valhalla, the armies will normally be 
left leaderless in the province they are in.  If Quintilian has the armies 
in a province you don't own, they will be transferred to your 
lowest-numbered leader in the same province, or at last resort, the garrison 
commander in an adjacent province owned by you.  If no leader is available, 
the armies will be disbanded.
  Quintilian can be given orders only for the first 2 phase(s) of the turn.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Lucky for this year.



  Here is the financial report for Lucky's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Lucky was left with 11 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Hecate
To: Lucky

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I prepared my forces to defend the Atl. Ocean 2008 and the 
surrounding provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Hecate


